The '''2025–26 South African Premiership''' was the 30th consecutive season of the [[South African Premiership]]. It was known as the '''Betway Premiership''' for sponsorship reasons, and also commonly referred to as the [[Premier Soccer League|PSL]] after the governing body.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ngidi |first=Njabulo |title=Betway bets on PSL with R900 million sponsorship: 'We don't chase away anybody,' says Khoza |url=https://www.news24.com/sport/soccer/psl/betway-bets-on-psl-with-r900-million-sponsorship-we-dont-chase-away-anybody-says-khoza-20240724 |access-date=2024-08-09 |website=Sport |language=en-US}}</ref>

The [[Orlando Pirates F.C.|Orlando Pirates]] won their fifth league title and first since the [[2011–12 South African Premiership]] season thus ending [[Mamelodi Sundowns F.C.|Mamelodi Sundowns]] reign as league champions. The [[Mamelodi Sundowns F.C.|Mamelodi Sundowns]] were defending the title they have won for eight consecutive years, the streak starting in the [[2017–18 South African Premiership|2017–18 season]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.timeslive.co.za/sport/soccer/2025-05-14-sundowns-crowned-league-champions-for-eighth-successive-season/|title=Sundowns crowned league champions for eighth successive season|accessdate=18 September 2025}}</ref> The [[Kaizer Chiefs]] drew an average home attendance of 20,347, the highest in the league.

==Teams==
=== Team changes ===
{{increase}} '''Promoted from [[2024–25 National First Division]]'''

* [[Durban City F.C. (2024)|Durban City]]<ref>{{Cite web |last=bulesitutshana |date=2025-06-12 |title=Durban City aim to grow fan base after promotion |url=https://witness.co.za/news/2025/06/12/durban-city-aim-to-grow-fan-base-after-promotion/ |access-date=2025-07-06 |website=The Witness |language=en-GB}}</ref>
* [[Orbit College F.C.|Orbit College]]<ref>{{Cite web |last=Vardien |first=Tashreeq |title=Little-known Orbit College FC seal dream promotion to PSL top flight as CT City relegated |url=https://www.news24.com/sport/soccer/psl/little-known-orbit-college-fc-seal-dream-promotion-to-psl-top-flight-as-ct-city-relegated-20250625-0952 |access-date=2025-07-06 |website=News24 |language=en-US}}</ref>

{{decrease}} '''Relegated to [[2025–26 National First Division]]'''

* [[Cape Town City F.C. (2016)|Cape Town City]]<ref>{{Cite web |last=Meletse |first=Obakeng |date=2013-11-28 |title=Relegation offers Cape Town City a chance to reset and refocus |url=https://iol.co.za/sport/soccer/psl/2025-07-01-relegation-offers-cape-town-city-a-chance-to-reset-and-refocus/ |access-date=2025-07-06 |website=IOL |language=en}}</ref>

{{decrease}} '''Expelled'''
* [[Royal AM F.C.|Royal AM]]<ref>{{Cite web |last=Vardien |first=Tashreeq |title=Royal AM out! PSL votes overwhelmingly to expel club from SA football |url=https://www.news24.com/sport/soccer/psl/psls-bog-vote-overwhelmingly-in-favour-of-royal-am-expulsion-20250410 |access-date=2025-04-10 |website=Sport |language=en-US}}</ref>

===Purchased statuses===
* [[Siwelele F.C.|Siwelele]] purchased the status from three-time champions [[SuperSport United F.C.|SuperSport United]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rabothe |first=Tshepo |date=2025-07-03 |title=SuperSport confirm status sale to Siwelele FC |url=https://farpost.co.za/2025/07/03/supersport-confirm-status-sale-to-siwelele-fc/ |access-date=2025-07-03 |website=FARPost |language=en-US}}</ref>

Orbit College and Siwelele will be playing in the Premiership for the first time. Durban City previously played as Maritzburg United.

